        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): wrap self-hosted discovery JSON parse in try/catch",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nWrap JSON.parse in readSelfHostedDiscoveryJson in try/catch so malformed JSON from self-hosted provider discovery produces a descriptive error with the endpoint label instead of a raw SyntaxError crash.\n\n## Real behavior proof (required for external PRs)\n\n**Behavior addressed**: JSON.parse on untrusted network response body without error handling.\n\n**Real environment tested**: Linux, Node 22, OpenClaw branch `fix/provider-self-hosted-setup-json-parse`\n\n**Proof command**:\n```bash\nnode_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/proof/provider-self-hosted-json-parse.mts\n```\n\n**Proof script output** (scripts/proof/provider-self-hosted-json-parse.mts):\n```\n=== Proof: self-hosted provider malformed discovery JSON ===\n\nEndpoint: http://127.0.0.1:46825/v1/models\nResponse body: not valid json {\n\n[plugins/self-hosted-provider-setup] Failed to discover malformed-test models: Error: malformed-test discovery response is not valid JSON\nDiscovered models: []\n\nPASS: malformed discovery JSON is caught and discovery returns an empty list.\n```\n\n**Regression test**:\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/provider-self-hosted-setup.test.ts\n```\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  13 passed (13)\n```\n\nThe regression test \"wraps malformed discovery JSON with a descriptive error\" now asserts the labeled warning is logged:\n- `mockedLogger.warn` is called once\n- the message contains `malformed-test discovery response is not valid JSON`\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. Called only during provider setup/discovery with existing caller-side error handling.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
